#
# MiSTer project
#
# WARNING WARNING WARNING:
# Do not add files to project in Quartus IDE! It will mess this file!
# Add the files manually to files.qip file.
#
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

set_global_assignment -name TOP_LEVEL_ENTITY sys_top
set_global_assignment -name PARTITION_NETLIST_TYPE SOURCE -section_id Top
set_global_assignment -name PARTITION_FITTER_PRESERVATION_LEVEL PLACEMENT_AND_ROUTING -section_id Top
set_global_assignment -name PARTITION_COLOR 16764057 -section_id Top

set_global_assignment -name LAST_QUARTUS_VERSION "17.0.0 Lite Edition"

set_global_assignment -name GENERATE_RBF_FILE ON
set_global_assignment -name PROJECT_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY output_files
set_global_assignment -name NUM_PARALLEL_PROCESSORS ALL
set_global_assignment -name SAVE_DISK_SPACE OFF
set_global_assignment -name SMART_RECOMPILE ON
set_global_assignment -name MIN_CORE_JUNCTION_TEMP "-40"
set_global_assignment -name MAX_CORE_JUNCTION_TEMP 100
set_global_assignment -name POWER_PRESET_COOLING_SOLUTION "23 MM HEAT SINK WITH 200 LFPM AIRFLOW"
set_global_assignment -name POWER_BOARD_THERMAL_MODEL "NONE (CONSERVATIVE)"
set_global_assignment -name TIMEQUEST_MULTICORNER_ANALYSIS OFF
set_global_assignment -name OPTIMIZE_POWER_DURING_FITTING OFF
set_global_assignment -name FINAL_PLACEMENT_OPTIMIZATION ALWAYS
# ROUTABILITY, WHICH THIS PROJECT HAD NEVER ASKED FOR.
#
# Adding the coprocessor took the design to 79% ALM / 82% M10K and the fitter
# stopped closing -- not on a shortage, but on ONE contended routing resource at
# a time, and a different one per seed (m2_pcm_fetch|buf_q, then i960 fp_a[55]
# and fp_b[56]). A single unroutable signal that MOVES between seeds is
# congestion, not capacity.
#
# THE AREA-MODE EXPERIMENT WAS RUN AND ABANDONED. Recorded so it is not
# repeated.
#
# Turning the four PHYSICAL_SYNTHESIS options off crashes this fitter --
# "Fatal Error: Segment Violation at (nil)" in
# TDB_NETLIST_ATOM_DELETOR::delete_tdb_objects_of_cell, immediately after
# placement succeeds -- four builds out of four, under both AGGRESSIVE AREA and
# BALANCED, with and without the router option. No resource numbers are written
# either, so the runs yield nothing at all.
#
# And it was not worth chasing. The Model 1 project measured Aggressive Area on
# its full core at 595 ALM saved for 11 M10K and the timing slack, and recorded
# "do not". 595 would not close this core's gap to the rasteriser anyway.
#
# The ALM the rasteriser needs comes from the design instead: the coprocessor's
# input queue is 128 x 32 bits of FLIP-FLOPS because the TGP reads its head
# asynchronously, which is about 2,000 ALM sitting in the resource we are short
# of. As an M10K FIFO with a registered read it costs one block, and we have
# ~101 spare.
#
# Previously: HIGH PERFORMANCE EFFORT,
# physical synthesis with combinational resynthesis, register duplication and
# retiming, plus router LCELL insertion. The fitter log shows what that costs --
# "Created 190 register duplicates" -- so the design was being told to spend
# routing to buy speed and then failed to route.
#
# This is Intel's own documented remedy for the error we get, and it was never
# set: "Guideline: Set Fitter Aggressive Routability Optimizations to Always".
# It may cost some Fmax, which is measurable; a design that does not fit is not.
# AUTOMATICALLY, NOT ALWAYS -- AND THE REASON IS THE FAILING PATH ITSELF.
#
# The worst path across several seeds is `hdmi_out_vs <= vs` in sys_top: two
# registers, same clock, NO LOGIC BETWEEN THEM. A bare flop-to-flop path can
# only fail on physical distance, which is why turning off
# PHYSICAL_SYNTHESIS_COMBO_LOGIC_FOR_AREA gave a byte-identical result -- there
# is nothing there to restructure. This option DELIBERATELY SPREADS LOGIC to
# relieve congestion, and spreading is exactly what pulls two adjacent flops
# apart. ALWAYS forces it everywhere; AUTOMATICALLY lets the fitter apply it
# where it is actually needed.
#
# It was added for a real failure -- the fitter could not route at all, on a
# different contended resource per seed -- so if routing fails again, this is
# the line to put back. Model 1 closes at 91% ALM against our 78%, so
# occupancy is not what is hurting us here.
#
# BACK TO ALWAYS, ON THIS FILE'S OWN CRITERION. The paragraph above ends "if
# routing fails again, this is the line to put back", and routing has failed
# again: the geometry pipeline took the design to 41,714 of 41,910 ALM and the
# fitter segfaulted in the router after placing at 99.5%.
#
# Two premises recorded above are now dead and are left in place as the record
# of how the setting was reasoned about when they were alive:
#   "Model 1 closes at 91% ALM against our 78%, so occupancy is not what is
#    hurting us here" -- our occupancy is now 99.5%, and it is exactly what is
#    hurting us.
#   The hdmi_out_vs flop-to-flop path was the argument against spreading logic.
#   A design that does not route has no Fmax to protect.
set_global_assignment -name FITTER_AGGRESSIVE_ROUTABILITY_OPTIMIZATION ALWAYS
set_global_assignment -name FITTER_EFFORT "STANDARD FIT"
# BALANCED, NOT AGGRESSIVE AREA. Aggressive Area crashed this fitter twice in
# succession -- "Fatal Error: Segment Violation at (nil)" after placement
# succeeded, with no resource numbers written either time. The speed-tuned
# builds get through placement AND routing and only fall over on exit, so this
# is a worse failure and not the usual Quartus 17 flakiness. The duplication
# settings below stay off, which is where most of the area comes from.
# AGGRESSIVE AREA. The paragraph above says it crashed this fitter twice; that
# was with ROUTER_LCELL_INSERTION_AND_LOGIC_DUPLICATION OFF, which the note
# below records as the difference between a crash after placement and a crash
# on exit. It is ON now.
#
# THE MODEL 1 PROJECT MEASURED THIS ON A FULL CORE AND ITS ANSWER WAS "DO NOT":
#
#     default (HIGH PERFORMANCE EFFORT / SPEED)  30,206 ALM  452 M10K  +0.331 ns
#     Aggressive Area / AREA                     29,611 ALM  463 M10K  +0.024 ns
#                                                   -595       +11
#
# -- "it trades the binding resource ... M10K is the binding resource here, 82%
# before this, 84% after, so it spends the scarce resource to save the plentiful
# one" (model1-ref/docs/findings.md).
#
# THAT REASONING INVERTS HERE, WHICH IS WHY WE TAKE THE SETTING THEY REJECTED.
# Ours is the opposite design: 99.5% ALM and 68% block memory. Spending M10K to
# buy ALM is precisely the trade we want and precisely the one they could not
# afford. The saving is small in absolute terms -- 2% on their core, so perhaps
# 800 ALM on ours -- and it is the timing that will decide this, not the area:
# they lost almost all their setup slack for it. Seed sweeping exists for that.
# BALANCED, AND THE OTHER FOUR AREA SETTINGS STAY. Aggressive Area WORKED on
# ALM -- 41,714 -> 37,109, 100% -> 89%, a saving of 4,605 -- and then the fitter
# segfaulted anyway, because of how it bought them:
#
#     Total RAM Blocks : 553 / 553 ( 100 % )
#     Total block memory bits : 4,282,232 / 5,662,720 ( 76 % )
#
# It moved logic into M10K during physical synthesis and filled every block on
# the device. m2_geometry uses ZERO M10K at synthesis, so the 3D work did not
# cause this -- the setting did, by spending the one resource we have least of.
#
# WHICH IS EXACTLY WHAT THE MODEL 1 PROJECT SAID IT WOULD DO. "It trades the
# binding resource ... it spends the scarce resource to save the plentiful one."
# The note above claims that reasoning inverts here because we are at 76% block
# memory; it does not. 76% is BITS. The binding number is RAM BLOCKS, and a
# memory too small to fill a block still costs a whole one -- 4,282,232 bits
# would fit in 418 blocks and 553 are allocated. That misreading is recorded
# rather than deleted because it is the second time this project has drawn a
# confident conclusion from the wrong column of a fitter report.
# BACK TO AGGRESSIVE AREA, AND THE FLOW IS NOW RUN STAGE BY STAGE.
#
# BALANCED was tried after this and crashed in 4 minutes at I/O placement --
# "Segment Violation at (nil)" with no resource numbers at all, which is a
# worse failure than Aggressive Area's. Aggressive Area reaches
#
#     Fitter Status : Successful
#     Logic utilization (in ALMs) : 37,109 / 41,910 ( 89 % )
#
# and only then segfaults ON EXIT. That is the survivable case this file
# already describes: the fit is committed, and quartus_sta and quartus_asm can
# finish the job on the database.
#
# THE DATABASE FROM THAT RUN WAS DESTROYED BY STARTING THE NEXT BUILD before
# checking whether it had left something usable. Do not do that again: after a
# fitter crash, run quartus_asm BEFORE launching anything else. `make rbf_rescue`
# exists for exactly this.
set_global_assignment -name OPTIMIZATION_MODE "AGGRESSIVE AREA"
set_global_assignment -name ALLOW_POWER_UP_DONT_CARE ON
set_global_assignment -name QII_AUTO_PACKED_REGISTERS NORMAL
# BACK ON, AND NOT BY PREFERENCE. With this OFF the fitter dies with
# "Fatal Error: Segment Violation at (nil)" immediately after placement, three
# builds out of three, under both AGGRESSIVE AREA and BALANCED. With it on the
# fitter completes placement AND routing and only falls over on exit, which is
# the survivable failure -- quartus_sta and quartus_asm then finish the job on
# the committed database. It is a ROUTER option and the crash is in routing.
# The physical-synthesis options stay off; they are where the area is.
set_global_assignment -name ROUTER_LCELL_INSERTION_AND_LOGIC_DUPLICATION ON
set_global_assignment -name PHYSICAL_SYNTHESIS_COMBO_LOGIC ON
set_global_assignment -name PHYSICAL_SYNTHESIS_REGISTER_DUPLICATION ON
set_global_assignment -name PHYSICAL_SYNTHESIS_REGISTER_RETIMING ON
# AREA, NOT SPEED. The whole of the block below was tuned when there were
# 8,940 ALM spare. There are 196.
# SPEED AGAIN, WITH AGGRESSIVE AREA KEPT. The two do different jobs and only
# one of them was hurting. AGGRESSIVE AREA + AREA fits at 36,961 ALM (88%) and
# MISSES TIMING on the 100 MHz SDRAM clock by -0.653 ns, TNS -5.895 -- which is
# not a marginal miss on a clock the whole core depends on.
#
# Model 1's measurement said this would happen: Aggressive Area "costs most of
# the timing margin", +0.331 ns -> +0.024 ns on their core. Ours went negative.
#
# So keep the mode that bought 4,600 ALM and put back the technique that pays
# for the paths. If this closes, the fit and the timing are both had; if it
# does not fit, the mode and the technique are not separable here and that is
# itself the answer.
# AREA. AGGRESSIVE AREA + SPEED was tried and produced nothing at all; AGGRESSIVE
# AREA + AREA is the only combination that has committed a fit and booted on
# hardware. It misses the 100 MHz SDRAM clock by -0.653 ns and the board runs
# anyway -- attract mode, sound, tilemap -- so the miss is real but not fatal at
# room temperature. Timing gets fixed by seed sweeping and by getting the
# occupancy down, not by a technique that cannot produce a bitstream.
set_global_assignment -name OPTIMIZATION_TECHNIQUE AREA
set_global_assignment -name MUX_RESTRUCTURE ON
set_global_assignment -name REMOVE_REDUNDANT_LOGIC_CELLS ON
set_global_assignment -name AUTO_DELAY_CHAINS_FOR_HIGH_FANOUT_INPUT_PINS ON
# OFF: a leftover from the area experiment this file says was ABANDONED.
# The design is in HIGH PERFORMANCE EFFORT with OPTIMIZATION_TECHNIQUE SPEED
# and 8,940 ALM spare, so area-targeted combinational restructuring is buying
# nothing and costing path depth. Turned off ALONE -- it is not one of the
# four whose removal segfaults this fitter, and the A/B is seed 19, which
# missed at -0.124 with it on.
# ON. The paragraph above justifies OFF with "the design is in HIGH PERFORMANCE
# EFFORT with OPTIMIZATION_TECHNIQUE SPEED and 8,940 ALM spare, so area-targeted
# combinational restructuring is buying nothing". Both halves of that are now
# false: the technique is AREA and the spare is 196 ALM.
set_global_assignment -name PHYSICAL_SYNTHESIS_COMBO_LOGIC_FOR_AREA ON
set_global_assignment -name ADV_NETLIST_OPT_SYNTH_WYSIWYG_REMAP ON
set_global_assignment -name SYNTH_GATED_CLOCK_CONVERSION ON
set_global_assignment -name PRE_MAPPING_RESYNTHESIS ON
set_global_assignment -name ROUTER_CLOCKING_TOPOLOGY_ANALYSIS ON
set_global_assignment -name ECO_OPTIMIZE_TIMING ON
set_global_assignment -name PERIPHERY_TO_CORE_PLACEMENT_AND_ROUTING_OPTIMIZATION ON
set_global_assignment -name PHYSICAL_SYNTHESIS_ASYNCHRONOUS_SIGNAL_PIPELINING ON
# HIGH, AND THIS IS THE ONE AIMED AT THE MEASURED PROBLEM. m2_geometry is
# 5,428 combinational ALUTs and 6,607 REGISTERS, and the total went from 33,195
# ALM to 41,714 -- about 4,000 ALM more than the parts account for. An ALM holds
# two combinational functions and four registers; above ~90% the fitter stops
# finding compatible pairs and spends a whole ALM on what should share one. The
# gap is packing collapse, so raise the packing effort.
set_global_assignment -name ALM_REGISTER_PACKING_EFFORT HIGH
set_global_assignment -name SEED 162

#set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "MISTER_FB=1"

#enable it only if 8bit indexed mode is used in core
#set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "MISTER_FB_PALETTE=1"

#do not enable DEBUG_NOHDMI in release!
#set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "MISTER_DEBUG_NOHDMI=1"

# disable bilinear filtering when downscaling
# ENABLED: ascal is 2,907 ALUTs and these two are cosmetic scaler features with
# no effect on what the game does. Cheapest area in the project -- they cost a
# slightly harder downscale and non-adaptive scanlines, nothing else.
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "MISTER_DOWNSCALE_NN=1"

# disable adaptive scanline filtering
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "MISTER_DISABLE_ADAPTIVE=1"

#use only 1MB per frame for scaler to free ~21MB DDR3 RAM
#set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "MISTER_SMALL_VBUF=1"

# Disable YC / Composite output to save some resources.
# ENABLED. Measured on the Model 1 core: a small ALM saving and a large slack
# gain, which is the ratio that matters here -- the fitter path is timing bound,
# not area bound. YC is the composite/S-Video encoder in sys_top.v; nothing in
# this core drives it and no output we use goes through it.
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "MISTER_DISABLE_YC=1"
# THE ON-SCREEN OVERLAY IS OFF, AND THE UART IS NOT. See Model2.sv's OVERLAY
# localparam. The geometry pipeline took the fit from 79% to "requires 4220
# LABs, the device contains only 4191"; m2_diag is 443.5 ALM and every finding
# since R136 came off /dev/ttyS1 rather than off the screen. m2_dbg_stream
# stays -- it is the only instrument that can say which memory the display
# list's objects point at, which is the question the 3D work now turns on.
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "M2_NO_OVERLAY=1"

# Disable ALSA audio output to save some resources.
# ENABLED, 251.5 ALM. ALSA is the HPS/Linux audio channel INTO audio_out's
# mixer, not an output: `core_l`/`core_r` carry this core's sound and sit
# outside the ifndef, and the analog jack is gated by MISTER_DUAL_SDRAM (not
# set) rather than by this. HDMI, the 3.5mm jack and S/PDIF all keep working.
# Model 2 has no CD or HPS-streamed audio, so nothing here ever fed it.
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "MISTER_DISABLE_ALSA=1"

# EXPERIMENT, NOT A FIX -- remove once it has answered.
# Keeps BUFFERRAM on and takes away ONLY the coprocessor's writes into shared
# buffer RAM. If 2D returns, the copro is corrupting the game's display list
# and the mapping was never at fault. See R139/R141.
# ANSWERED: with copro writes off the board still spun, so the coprocessor is
# not corrupting the display list. Removed.
#set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "M2_NO_COPRO_BUFW=1"

# EXPERIMENT, NOT A FIX -- remove once it has answered.
# BUFFERRAM stays mapped and the CPU's WRITES still land, but its READS return
# 0 exactly as in the working .attract build. Splits "the mapping is wrong"
# from "what the CPU reads back is wrong" in one build.
# ANSWERED: reads->0 restored the machine and woke the walker. It is the
# i960's READS of buffer RAM at fault, not the mapping and not its writes. R141.
#set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "M2_BUFFERRAM_WRONLY=1"

# EXPERIMENT, NOT A FIX -- remove once it has answered.
# BUFFERRAM fully on (reads enabled again) with the geometrizer front door's
# push DMA into buffer RAM disabled. The last writer of that memory not yet
# cleared by experiment; same shape as the copro test that exonerated 35d991a9.
# ANSWERED: with the front door's writes off the board still spun. NOTHING
# that writes buffer RAM is at fault -- copro and front door both cleared by
# experiment. The read path itself is. R141.
#set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "M2_NO_GEO_BUFW=1"

source sys/sys.tcl
source sys/sys_analog.tcl
source files.qip
